      "name": "Pushin CLI v0.3.4",
      "tag": "v0.3.4",
      "body": "\n### Added\n\n- GitHub CLI command paths for `repo list`, `repo edit`, `repo license list`,\n  `issue list`, `issue view`, and `release delete-asset`, with supported filters,\n  pagination, human-readable output, and JSON projection. Repository visibility\n  changes require `--accept-visibility-change-consequences`, matching `gh`.\n- Support for `--json fields` alongside `--json=fields` and bare `--json`.\n- Named `hook`, `ruleset`, `runner`, `org-runner`, `runner-group`,\n  `org-runner-group`, and `notification` commands, including webhook config,\n  tests, secret rotation, delivery inspection, and redelivery.\n- An executable `api-endpoints.json` catalog covering all versioned API\n  operations through `pun endpoint`. The same catalog can be pinned by the\n  server to fail its offline parity test when endpoints change.\n- `pun run` commands to inspect workflow runs, jobs, logs, workflow metadata,\n  artifacts, and combined commit status; rerun workflows or failed jobs and\n  their dependants; cancel runs; and download log and artifact ZIP archives.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Login uses token introspection and accepts scoped PATs without Account read,\n  while status reads the account profile from `/user`. Without Account read,\n  status falls back to token introspection and shows the login, masked token,\n  permissions and repository access instead of failing. Both commands explain\n  that Account read enables the full profile. Terminal token input is hidden.\n  Older servers receive an actionable permission hint; other authentication,\n  blocked-account, rate-limit and server errors remain errors.\n- JSON field names are validated before requests. A word after `--json` is\n  always the field list, so put positional arguments first. Bare `--json` last\n  or before another flag prints the full response; `pun --json pr list` also\n  works.\n- Unknown JSON fields report the available keys in sorted order and exit with\n  status 1, explaining that the command completed and only JSON output failed.\n  List fields must occur in at least one item; empty lists and scalar responses\n  (including null from a successful empty response) pass through unchanged.\n- A shorter README quickstart with updated command examples and scoped-token\n  login guidance.\n- Automated releases use workflow job tokens to publish CLI releases.\n\n",
      "url": "https://pushin.eu/pjullrich/pushin-cli/releases/tag/v0.3.4",
